# Line endings: store every text file with LF (Unix style) in the repo, whatever the computer.
# Windows git (core.autocrlf=true) was printing "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every add.
# "text=auto" lets git decide what is text; "eol=lf" keeps LF in your working copy too,
# so the files on disk match what GitHub, the validator and the browser see.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never convert line endings and never try to diff or merge them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
